+/* AN ALERT OVER A DIALOG IS A CARD OF ITS OWN (audit, 21 Nov 2026). The kit's alert has no edge: it stands out by the dimmed page behind it. But its scrim is under an open dialog (9990 against the dialog's 9992), so "Leave this group?" raised from Group members was a white card on a white card, a hole in the dialog with its rows cut off on either side. The alert's scrim comes over the dialog (the kit appends it just before the card, and after any dialog), and the card has a hairline and a shadow wherever it stands. */
+.un-backdrop:has(+ .un-alert) { z-index: 9992; }
+html:not([data-skin]) .un-alert { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--app-sheet-line), 0 18px 48px -18px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.45); }
